[727.700342, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[1;30r\u001b[30;1H\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K\u001b[2m• \u001b[22mThe first complete run resolves 118 of 119 rows, matches 793 fields, and flags 18 properties with\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  114.802 ha of relevant post-2020 loss. Two cattle properties have a qualifying slaughter-point\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  override; the rest retain their municipality cooperative. I spotted one subtle contact issue in\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  validation—municipality candidates must key to the CAR municipality code, not merely whichever\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[39;49m\u001b[K  municipality polygon contains the parcel centroid—and I’m correcting that before finalizing the\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
